    {
        "content": "<p>A second, unrelated <code>fun_prop</code> issue: it ignores a hypothesis that is literally the goal, when the function is a field of a structure-valued <code>def</code> whose value is a lambda of at least two arguments:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⟨</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">⟩</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- fails: No theorems found for `g` in order to prove `Differentiable ℝ fun x =&gt; g x i`</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Differentiable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">myP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Differentiable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">myP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- works: a variable in place of `myP g`</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Differentiable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A.val</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Differentiable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A.val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- works: the field value is not a lambda</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myP'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Differentiable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">myP'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Differentiable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">myP'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myQ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⟨</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">⟩</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- works: one-argument lambda body</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Differentiable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">myQ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Differentiable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">myQ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It also works if the field is <code>ℝ → ℝ</code> with a one-argument lambda body.</p>\n<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n<p>diagnosis by Claude</p>\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<p>The cause appears to be that <code>Mor.whnfPred</code> calls <code>whnfCore</code>, whose default <code>proj := .yesWithDelta</code> unfolds <code>myP g</code> to reduce the projection. So <code>(myP g).val</code> becomes the body <code>fun x i =&gt; g x i</code>. After applying <code>x</code> this is still a lambda, so <code>getFunctionData?</code> returns <code>.lam</code>. The goal then goes straight to the pi rule, while the hypothesis <code>h</code> (which unfolds the same way) is dropped by the <code>| return none</code> in <code>getLocalTheorems</code>. With a one-argument body you get <code>.data</code> with head <code>g</code> on both sides, and they match.</p>\n<p>Possible fixes, untested: reduce projections without delta (<code>proj := .yes</code>) in <code>whnfPred</code>, or check local hypotheses before unfolding.</p>\n</div></div>\n<p>I hit this with Physlib's <code>harmonicWaveX</code>, a structure-valued <code>def</code> whose field is <code>fun x μ =&gt; match μ with ...</code>.</p>",
        "id": 627268699,
        "sender_full_name": "ZhiKai Pong",
        "timestamp": 1790546975
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The second bug is fixed in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/35548\">#35548</a>, which prevents <code>myP</code> from getting unfolded.</p>",
        "id": 627463639,
        "sender_full_name": "Attila Gáspár",
        "timestamp": 1790607302
    }
]